---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import StackedBars from '../../../components/StackedBars.svelte';
import LineSeries from '../../../components/LineSeries.svelte';
import ValueBars from '../../../components/ValueBars.svelte';
import SmallMultiples from '../../../components/SmallMultiples.svelte';
import ChartFilters from '../../../components/ChartFilters.svelte';
import { readData, href } from '../../../lib/data';
import { exceptionsUsedBy } from '../../../lib/exceptions';
import { referenceFor } from '../../../lib/reference';
import { dollars, fyLabel } from '../../../lib/format';
import { millions } from '../../../lib/chart';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  const { entities } = readData('index.json');
  return entities.filter((e: any) => e.datasets.includes('ws_summary')).map((e: any) => ({ params: { entity: e.entity_id } }));
}
const entity = '' + Astro.params.entity;
const meta = readData(entity, 'meta.json');
const palette = readData('palette.json');
const all: any[] = readData(entity, 'ws_summary.json').rows;
const dept: any[] = readData(entity, 'ws_audit_vs_budget.json').rows;
const exceptions = exceptionsUsedBy(entity, all);
const ref = referenceFor(entity);
const exDept = exceptionsUsedBy(entity, dept);
const audited = all.filter((r) => r.net_position_total != null);
const first = audited[0], last = audited.at(-1)!;
const budget = all.find((r) => r.fiscal_year === last.fiscal_year + 1 && r.budget_revenues != null);
const years = audited.map((r) => r.fiscal_year);

const peak = audited.reduce((a, b) => (b.net_position_total > a.net_position_total ? b : a));
const low = audited.filter((r) => r.fiscal_year > peak.fiscal_year).reduce((a, b) => (b.net_position_total < a.net_position_total ? b : a));
const negIncome = audited.filter((r) => r.operating_income < 0);
const capEx = audited.filter((r) => r.purchases_of_capital_assets > r.cash_flow_operating);
const budgetary = audited.filter((r) => r.budgetary_expenses_actual != null);
let since = budgetary.at(-1)!.fiscal_year;  // the first year of the unbroken run of expenses above revenues that ends with the latest audit
for (const r of [...budgetary].reverse()) { if (r.budgetary_expenses_actual > r.budgetary_revenues_actual) since = r.fiscal_year; else break; }
const advance = last.cash_flow_noncapital_financing;

const series = (key: string, name: string) => audited.filter((r) => r[key] != null).map((r) => ({ fiscal_year: r.fiscal_year, series: name, value: r[key], exception_ids: r.exception_ids }));
const npRows = [...series('net_position_net_investment_in_capital', 'Invested in capital assets'), ...series('net_position_restricted', 'Restricted'),
  ...series('net_position_unrestricted', 'Unrestricted')].filter((r) => r.value);
const incomeRows = [...series('budgetary_revenues_actual', 'Operating revenues'), ...series('budgetary_expenses_actual', 'Operating expenses (budgetary basis)')];
const cashRows = series('cash_and_investments_comparable', 'Cash and investments');
const opRows = [...series('cash_flow_operating', 'Cash from operations'), ...series('purchases_of_capital_assets', 'Capital assets bought')];
const gaapRows = audited.map((r) => ({ fiscal_year: r.fiscal_year, value: r.operating_income, exception_ids: r.exception_ids }));
const changeRows = audited.map((r) => ({ fiscal_year: r.fiscal_year, value: r.change_in_net_position, exception_ids: r.exception_ids }));
const deptRows = dept.map((r) => ({ fiscal_year: r.fiscal_year, group: r.department, budget: r.audit_original, actual: r.audit_actual, exception_ids: r.exception_ids }));
const comparable = dept.filter((r) => r.diff != null), agree = comparable.filter((r) => r.diff === 0).length;
const misses = comparable.filter((r) => r.diff !== 0);
const exById = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(exDept));
const pct = (v: number) => `${v >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${(v * 100).toFixed(0)}%`;
---
<Base entity={entity} section="water-sewer" title={`Water and Sewer Fund – ${meta.short_name}`} description={`${meta.name}: Water and Sewer Fund net position, operating results, cash and audited spending against budget.`}>
  <p class="muted"><a href={href(`/${entity}/`)}>{meta.short_name}</a> › Water and Sewer</p>
  <h1>Water and Sewer Fund</h1>
  <p class="muted">The city's utility, paid for by user charges and kept apart from the General Fund. From the audits {fyLabel(first.fiscal_year)}–{fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)} (year ends April 30) and the budget ordinances. Its statements use business-style accounting, with depreciation and net position instead of a fund balance.</p>

  <dl class="summary">
    <div><dt>{fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)} net position</dt><dd>{millions(last.net_position_total, 1)}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Operating revenues</dt><dd>{millions(last.operating_revenues, 1)}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Operating income, after depreciation</dt><dd>{millions(last.operating_income, 1)}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Cash and investments</dt><dd>{millions(last.cash_and_investments_comparable, 1)}</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>What stands out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Net position, what the utility owns less what it owes, was {millions(first.net_position_total, 1)} in {fyLabel(first.fiscal_year)}, peaked at {millions(peak.net_position_total, 1)} in {fyLabel(peak.fiscal_year)}, fell to {millions(low.net_position_total, 1)} in {fyLabel(low.fiscal_year)} and was {millions(last.net_position_total, 1)} in {fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)}.</li>
    <li>After depreciation the utility lost money on operations in {negIncome.length} of {audited.length} years ({fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)}: {millions(last.operating_income, 1)}). Net position rose in {fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)} anyway, by {millions(last.change_in_net_position, 1)}, because of capital grants and contributions.</li>
    <li>On the city's budgetary basis, which counts capital outlay as spending, expenses have exceeded operating revenues every year since {fyLabel(since)} ({fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)}: {millions(last.budgetary_expenses_actual, 1)} against {millions(last.budgetary_revenues_actual, 1)}).</li>
    <li>Capital assets bought exceeded cash from operations in {capEx.length} of {audited.length} years. Cash and investments {advance ? `rose to ${millions(last.cash_and_investments_comparable, 1)} in ${fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)} after a ${millions(advance, 1)} advance from the General Fund` : `were ${millions(last.cash_and_investments_comparable, 1)} in ${fyLabel(last.fiscal_year)}`}.</li>
    {budget && <li>The adopted {fyLabel(budget.fiscal_year)} budget has revenues of {millions(budget.budget_revenues, 2)} and expenses of {millions(budget.budget_expenses, 2)}.</li>}
  </ul>

  <ChartFilters client:load years={years} showDept={false} unitBase={ref?.base ?? null} />
  <p class="muted small-note">The year range and the Dollars choice are saved in the page address and apply to every chart below. “Per resident” divides by the whole city's population, not by the utility's customers.</p>

  <h2>Revenues and spending</h2>
  <LineSeries client:load id="income" exceptions={exceptions} units={ref?.units} rows={incomeRows} series={[{ name: 'Operating revenues', color: '#1baf7a' }, { name: 'Operating expenses (budgetary basis)', color: '#eb6834' }]}
    kind="money" title="Operating revenues and expenses, budgetary basis" filename="water-sewer-revenues-expenses.csv"
    note="From the audit's budget-and-actual schedule: expenses include capital outlay and leave out depreciation, the way the city budgets." />
  <ValueBars client:load id="operating-income" exceptions={exceptions} units={ref?.units} rows={gaapRows} up={palette.up} down={palette.down} ink={palette.ink} valueLabel="Operating income ($)"
    title="Operating income after depreciation" filename="water-sewer-operating-income.csv"
    note="The statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position: operating revenues minus operating expenses including depreciation." />

  <h2>Net position</h2>
  <StackedBars client:load id="net-position" exceptions={exceptions} units={ref?.units} ink={palette.ink} rows={npRows} totalLabel="Net position"
    series={[{ name: 'Invested in capital assets', color: '#2a78d6' }, { name: 'Restricted', color: '#eda100' }, { name: 'Unrestricted', color: '#1baf7a' }]}
    title="Net position by component" filename="water-sewer-net-position.csv"
    note="Invested in capital assets: plants, pipes and equipment less the debt that paid for them. Restricted: set aside for bond payments. Unrestricted: available for any utility use. FY2012-13 call this 'net assets'." />
  <ValueBars client:load id="net-change" exceptions={exceptions} units={ref?.units} rows={changeRows} up={palette.up} down={palette.down} ink={palette.ink} valueLabel="Change in net position ($)"
    title="Change in net position" filename="water-sewer-net-position-change.csv"
    note="Includes capital grants and contributions, which is why it can be positive when operating income is not." />

  <h2>Cash</h2>
  <LineSeries client:load id="cash" exceptions={exceptions} units={ref?.units} rows={cashRows} series={[{ name: 'Cash and investments', color: '#2a78d6' }]}
    kind="money" title="Cash and investments" filename="water-sewer-cash.csv"
    note="FY2012 is shown on the same footing as later years (including a $4.3M investments line the FY2012 cash flow statement leaves out)." />
  <LineSeries client:load id="capital" exceptions={exceptions} units={ref?.units} rows={opRows} series={[{ name: 'Cash from operations', color: '#1baf7a' }, { name: 'Capital assets bought', color: '#eb6834' }]}
    kind="money" title="Cash from operations vs capital assets bought" filename="water-sewer-cash-flow.csv"
    note="Net cash from operating activities, and purchases of capital assets from the cash flow statement." />

  <h2>Audited spending against the budget</h2>
  <SmallMultiples client:load units={ref?.units} exceptions={exDept} rows={deptRows}
    groups={[{ name: 'Water', color: '#2a78d6' }, { name: 'Sewer', color: '#eb6834' }, { name: 'Collection system', color: '#1baf7a' }]}
    ink={palette.ink} ink2={palette.ink2} surface={palette.surface} title="Original budget (line) and audited actual operating expenses (dots), by department" />
  <p>The audit's original budget equals the budget document's expense lines, without the depreciation and bond set-asides, transfers out and the card-processing fee, in {agree} of {comparable.length} comparable department-years. The {misses.length} that differ:</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Fiscal year</th><th>Department</th><th class="num">Audit original</th><th class="num">Budget on the audit's footing</th><th class="num">Difference</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{misses.map((r: any) => (
      <tr><td>{fyLabel(r.fiscal_year)}</td><td>{r.department}</td><td class="num">{dollars(r.audit_original)}</td><td class="num">{dollars(r.budget_adjusted)}</td><td class="num">{dollars(r.diff)}</td>
        <td>{r.exception_ids.filter((id: string) => id.startsWith('EX-ws-audit-')).map((id: string) => <span><strong>{id}</strong>: {exById[id]?.summary}. </span>)}</td></tr>
    ))}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="muted">The budget documents' cash sub-ledgers (bond reserves, connection fees, depreciation funding) are not on the site yet. Data: <a href={href(`/data/${entity}/ws_summary.json`)}>Water/Sewer by year</a> · <a href={href(`/data/${entity}/ws_audit_vs_budget.json`)}>audit vs budget</a> · <a href={href(`/data/${entity}/downloads/facts.csv.gz`)}>all extracted lines</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .summary { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin: 16px 0 8px; }
  .summary div { background: var(--panel); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .summary dt { color: var(--ink2); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .summary dd { margin: 0; font-size: 1.375rem; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .small-note { font-size: 0.8125rem; margin-top: 6px; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  td.num, th.num { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
